WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:07.001
This is our Earth, and this is our Sun.

2
00:00:07.221 --> 00:00:10.286
What is Earth made of? And
what does the Sun give us?

3
00:00:10.786 --> 00:00:14.129
Start at your house. Now zoom
out, and there is your town.

4
00:00:14.349 --> 00:00:17.275
Zoom out again, and there
is your whole country.

5
00:00:17.495 --> 00:00:23.718
Zoom out once more. There is the whole
Earth, a round planet floating in space.

6
00:00:23.938 --> 00:00:27.793
Earth is the planet we live on.
Everyone you know lives on it.

7
00:00:28.013 --> 00:00:32.935
The ground looks flat, because Earth
is so big. From space, it is round.

8
00:00:33.435 --> 00:00:36.268
Look at Earth from space.
Most of it is blue.

9
00:00:36.488 --> 00:00:40.668
Blue is water. That is
the sea. Green is land.

10
00:00:40.888 --> 00:00:45.717
Is there more water, or more land?
Catch a globe ten times to find out.

11
00:00:45.937 --> 00:00:51.371
Each time, look under your finger. Is
it on blue water, or on green land?

12
00:00:51.591 --> 00:00:55.074
Seven catches landed on
water, and three on land.

13
00:00:55.294 --> 00:00:59.009
There is more water than
land. Earth is mostly water.

14
00:00:59.509 --> 00:01:02.249
What is land made of? Dig
down through the grass.

15
00:01:02.469 --> 00:01:07.020
First there is soil, dark and
crumbly. Plants grow in it.

16
00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:11.513
In the soil are small stones. A
stone is a tiny piece of rock.

17
00:01:11.733 --> 00:01:15.494
Dig deeper. The soil runs
out, and you hit hard rock.

18
00:01:15.714 --> 00:01:19.476
So land is soil on top, and
rock underneath, everywhere.

19
00:01:19.696 --> 00:01:24.897
A pebble is a small piece of rock.
A mountain is a huge piece of rock.

20
00:01:25.397 --> 00:01:29.484
At night there is no Sun. It
is dark, and it is cooler.

21
00:01:29.704 --> 00:01:32.676
The Sun rises, and light fills the sky.

22
00:01:32.896 --> 00:01:37.958
At midday the Sun is high. It warms
the ground, the sea and your skin.

23
00:01:38.178 --> 00:01:41.707
Put one cup of water in the
sun. Put one in the shade.

24
00:01:41.927 --> 00:01:46.711
Wait an hour. The cup in the sun gets
warmer. The shade one stays cool.

25
00:01:46.931 --> 00:01:51.435
The Sun is a source of light and
heat. Both come from the Sun.

26
00:01:51.655 --> 00:01:56.253
Never look straight at the Sun. It
is so bright it can hurt your eyes.

27
00:01:56.753 --> 00:02:00.700
At night the sky is full of
tiny lights. They are stars.

28
00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:05.564
Each star is a huge ball of
hot, glowing gas, very far away.

29
00:02:05.784 --> 00:02:10.150
The Sun is a star too. It looks
big because it is the nearest one.

30
00:02:10.370 --> 00:02:13.156
Earth is our planet. The Sun is our star.

31
00:02:13.656 --> 00:02:17.185
Earth is the planet we live
on. Most of it is water.

32
00:02:17.405 --> 00:02:19.867
Land is soil on top, and rock underneath.

33
00:02:20.087 --> 00:02:24.266
The Sun gives us light and
heat. It is our nearest star.

34
00:02:24.486 --> 00:02:26.808
Now you know your Earth and your Sun.
